# AssemblyAI

Before writing AssemblyAI code, fetch https://www.assemblyai.com/docs/agent-instructions.md and https://www.assemblyai.com/docs/llms.txt. Do not trust memorized params.

Use the official `assemblyai` JS SDK (`npm i assemblyai@latest`) unless the Voice Agent WebSocket has no SDK helper — then follow live Voice Agent API docs.

## Auth

- REST `/v2/*`, streaming STT token + WS, LLM Gateway: `Authorization: <raw key>` (no Bearer).
- Voice Agent API token + WS (`agents.assemblyai.com`): `Authorization: Bearer <key>`.
- Browser/mobile: mint a single-use temp token on the server. Never ship the project key.

## Models and deprecations

- Default STT: `universal-3-5-pro` (streaming: `speech_model`; pre-recorded: `speech_models: ["universal-3-5-pro", "universal-2"]`).
- Forbidden: LeMUR, `auto_chapters`, `summarization`, `summary_model`, `summary_type`, `u3-rt-pro`, hallucinated SDK enums.
- Summaries, action items, chapters: transcribe first, then LLM Gateway (`claude-sonnet-4-6` or current IDs from docs).
- Always `Terminate` streaming STT sessions.

## This product

Live talk: Voice Agent API (or streaming STT + Gateway if we need custom TTS). Post-call: pre-recorded STT with `speaker_labels`, then Gateway for brief + promises. Keyterms: Pocketless, person names, product terms.
